\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Divergence and the discrete Poisson equation}
\date{2026-11-03}


\p{The [incidence matrix](fdip-00AF) #{B} is the difference matrix of
the preceding discussion, and #{L=B^{\mathsf T}B} is the graph
Laplacian. The matrix #{-B^{\mathsf T}} is the discrete divergence.
With the edge field #{E=-B\varphi}, Gauss's law #{\nabla\cdot E=\rho}
becomes
##{\,(-B^{\mathsf T})(-B\varphi)=B^{\mathsf T}B\varphi=L\varphi=\rho,}
the discrete Poisson equation. Computations, and the later Laplacian
chapters, use #{d} in this matrix form.}
